-- title:
--   Theorem 2.3 — asymmetric Lovász Local Lemma (variable setting), with the product lower bound
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal V$ be a finite family of mutually independent random variables on a probability space, and $\mathcal E$ a finite family of (bad) events. Each $E \in \mathcal E$ is determined by a set $\mathrm{vbl}(E) \subseteq \mathcal V$ of variables, and $\Gamma(E)$ is the set of the other events $F \in \mathcal E$ with $\mathrm{vbl}(F) \cap \mathrm{vbl}(E) \neq \emptyset$. Suppose numbers $x(E) \in (0,1)$ satisfy
--
--   $$\Pr[E] \le x(E) \prod_{F \in \Gamma(E)} \big(1 - x(F)\big) \quad \text{for every } E \in \mathcal E. \tag{5}$$
--
--   Then
--
--   $$\Pr\Big[\bigcap_{E \in \mathcal E} \overline{E}\Big] \ge \prod_{E \in \mathcal E} \big(1 - x(E)\big) > 0. \tag{6}$$
--
--   This is the local lemma of Moser and Tardos's variable setting, used in §4 to find one choice vector avoiding every long bad event simultaneously.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The probability space is an arbitrary $(\Omega, \mu)$ with $\mu$ a probability measure. The variables are measurable maps $X_v : \Omega \to \beta_v$ ($v$ in a finite type $V$, arbitrary measurable target spaces) that are mutually independent (`iIndepFun`). The events are a family $E : \iota \to \mathrm{Set}\,\Omega$ over a finite index type $\iota$; "$E_i$ is determined by $\mathrm{vbl}(i)$" is: $E_i$ is measurable for the $\sigma$-algebra generated by the $X_v$, $v \in \mathrm{vbl}(i)$ (`⨆ v ∈ vbl i, comap (X v)`). $\Gamma(i)$ is the set of indices $j \ne i$ with $\mathrm{vbl}(j) \cap \mathrm{vbl}(i)$ nonempty. Probabilities are `μ.real`.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: a finite family of events E with Γ(E) the other events → an indexed family E : ι → Set Ω over a finite type, Γ(i) = indices j ≠ i sharing a variable; reason: standard indexing of a finite family; a family without repetitions is a special instance and repeated events only add hypotheses
--   - encoding: vbl(E) a set of variables determining E → E i measurable for the σ-algebra generated by the X v, v ∈ vbl i; reason: the measure-theoretic meaning of 'determined by'
--   - encoding: random variables → measurable maps X v into arbitrary measurable spaces, mutually independent (iIndepFun); reason: the definition of a family of mutually independent random variables
--   - encoding: Pr[⋂ Ē] ≥ ∏(1 − x(E)) > 0 → the conjunction ∏(1 − x i) ≤ μ.real (⋂ (E i)ᶜ) ∧ 0 < ∏(1 − x i); reason: the printed chain of two inequalities as a conjunction
-- source:
--   Xu, Fu, Qiao, Tao, Synchronization Strings over a Ternary Alphabet, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 1b74ae6d…), p. 14 (PDF 15), §2.2, Theorem 2.3

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace TernarySync.Alphabet

/-- Theorem 2.3, the asymmetric Lovász Local Lemma in the variable setting (§2.2, p. 14).
`X v` (`v ∈ V`, `V` finite) are mutually independent random variables on a probability space
`(Ω, μ)` with values in arbitrary measurable spaces. `E i` (`i ∈ ι`, `ι` finite) are the bad
events; `E i` is determined by the variables `vbl i ⊆ V`, i.e. it is measurable for the
σ-algebra they generate. `Γ(i)` is the set of the other indices `j ≠ i` with
`vbl j ∩ vbl i ≠ ∅`. If `x i ∈ (0, 1)` and `Pr[E i] ≤ x i ∏_{j ∈ Γ(i)} (1 − x j)` for every `i`,
then `Pr[⋂_i (E i)ᶜ] ≥ ∏_i (1 − x i) > 0`. -/
theorem theorem_2_3 {Ω : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
    {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V] {β : V → Type*} [∀ v, MeasurableSpace (β v)]
    (X : ∀ v, Ω → β v) (hXm : ∀ v, Measurable (X v)) (hind : iIndepFun X μ)
    {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] (E : ι → Set Ω) (vbl : ι → Finset V)
    (hdet : ∀ i, MeasurableSet[⨆ v ∈ vbl i, MeasurableSpace.comap (X v) inferInstance] (E i))
    (x : ι → ℝ) (hx : ∀ i, 0 < x i ∧ x i < 1)
    (h5 : ∀ i, μ.real (E i) ≤
      x i * ∏ j ∈ Finset.univ.filter (fun j => j ≠ i ∧ (vbl j ∩ vbl i).Nonempty), (1 - x j)) :
    ∏ i, (1 - x i) ≤ μ.real (⋂ i, (E i)ᶜ) ∧ 0 < ∏ i, (1 - x i) := by sorry

end TernarySync.Alphabet
